# Teachable Machine Image Classifier

## Overview

This project explores the basics of Machine Learning using Google's Teachable Machine.

The goal was to train a simple image classifier with two categories and understand how data quality and quantity affect model performance.

## Categories Used

* Class 1: Pen
* Class 2: Mobile Phone

*(Replace these with your actual categories if different.)*

## Objective

* Train a classifier using Teachable Machine
* Observe model behavior with different amounts of training data
* Test the impact of noisy and inconsistent data
* Record observations about model learning

## Tools Used

* Google Teachable Machine
* Web Browser
* Camera / Image Samples

## Training Process

### Initial Training

* Added a small number of images for each class.
* Trained the model.
* Observed moderate accuracy.

### Improved Training

* Added more images from different angles and lighting conditions.
* Retrained the model.
* Accuracy improved significantly.

### Noisy Data Experiment

* Added unclear and inconsistent images.
* Retrained the model.
* Accuracy decreased and predictions became less reliable.

## Results

The model successfully classified the two categories when sufficient and consistent training data was provided.

The classifier performed best when:

* Images were clear.
* Training samples were balanced.
* Different viewing angles were included.

## Observations

### Observation 1

More training data improves model performance because the model sees more examples and learns better patterns.

### Observation 2

High-quality and consistent images lead to more accurate predictions than blurry or noisy images.

### Observation 3

Balanced datasets are important. If one class has significantly more images than another, predictions may become biased.

## What I Learned

* Machine learning depends heavily on data quality.
* More data generally improves accuracy.
* Noisy and inconsistent data can confuse a model.
* Training a model is not only about algorithms but also about preparing good data.

